{"uid":"21fb744f38a29510","name":"test_a_mix_of_curable_and_incurable_gate_findings_ends_the_run_with_an_approach_left","fullName":"tests.test_peer_verdict_gate#test_a_mix_of_curable_and_incurable_gate_findings_ends_the_run_with_an_approach_left","historyId":"0f963f59bd01fbab289b7ed044069df8","time":{"start":1791915608067,"stop":1791915608147,"duration":80},"description":"Task 001 (PRD requirement A.1/A.2, #192, this wave's v0.21.1\n    requirement A): the exact scenario the requirement's own `Cured when:`\n    clause names -- \"a real cloned supervisor at approach 1 of 2, given a\n    verdict-gate rejection carrying one curable AND one non-curable\n    blocking finding\" -- but this time with an approach still available\n    (`max_approaches=2`, approach 1 of 2), the case v0.21's own shipped\n    `test_a_mix_of_curable_and_incurable_gate_findings_still_ends_the_run`\n    above never drove because it fixed `max_approaches=1`. Before task\n    001's fix this returned `('advance', 'replan', 'verdict_gate_\n    rejected_approach_left')` -- it archived approach 1 and started a\n    fresh planning phase over a non-curable finding no fresh approach can\n    change. After the fix it must end `failed`/`unverified` right there,\n    with no approach archive, no `replan` phase and no appended cure\n    task -- exactly A.1 and A.2's own wording.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 001 (PRD requirement A.1/A.2, #192, this wave's v0.21.1<br />\nrequirement A): the exact scenario the requirement's own <code>Cured when:</code><br />\nclause names -- &quot;a real cloned supervisor at approach 1 of 2, given a<br />\nverdict-gate rejection carrying one curable AND one non-curable<br />\nblocking finding&quot; -- but this time with an approach still available<br />\n(<code>max_approaches=2</code>, approach 1 of 2), the case v0.21's own shipped<br />\n<code>test_a_mix_of_curable_and_incurable_gate_findings_still_ends_the_run</code><br />\nabove never drove because it fixed <code>max_approaches